 ### [Spatially Constrained Optimization](13691-spatially-constrained-optimization.md)
-[Spatially Constrained Optimization](13691-spatially-constrained-optimization.md) is a post-processing constraint workflow that applies an opacity loss to force full opacity rendering of target objects, followed by the re-initialization of boundary primitives that retain low opacity to clean up artifacts. It sets itself apart from standard pruning methods by preserving transparent primitives via re-initialization rather than removal, ensuring full coverage and stabilizing optimization in complex regions.
